# RFC #362 desktop.11 (Windows distribution patch, also valid upstream):
#
# Export/render busy signal, decoupled from presentation class names.
#
# The Windows host must know when an export or render is in flight (quit
# confirmation, tray busy). Reading .cw-render-status / .cw-timeline-pending
# class names from Host.cs tied that decision to markup that can be renamed
# at any time. The app now publishes one contract: while at least one
# export or render is in flight, the document element carries
# `data-od-exporting`; when none is, the attribute is absent. The signal is
# refcounted (overlapping exports must not clear it early) and covers the
# timeline output card (rendering/publishing phases only — a failed or
# finished card is not exporting), the stage editor's MP4 render and the
# timeline editor's package/render runs. Hosts read the attribute first and
# may keep the old class selector as a fallback for older bundles;
# Electron-style shells exposing window.opendirectorDesktop.setExporting
# also observe the transitions (same bridge shape as upstream PR #397).
#
# Also folds in the render-error guidance the failure-state inventory
# asked for: the H.264/AAC encoder errors now tell Windows N/KN users to
# install the Media Feature Pack (bilingual, kept in the message catalogs
# where the rest of the wording lives).
#
# No storage, render or model business rule is touched: this is a
# presentation-side signal plus two message strings.
